###Relational

// ============================================================================================
// firm_balance_sheet::Store -- 26 tables and 4 aggregation views in the `fbs` SCHEMA
// ============================================================================================
// THE SCHEMA, which is one of the two constructs this project is here to carry. Everything
// this project owns lives in `fbs` and not in the default schema, and that is not tidiness:
//
//   * A published balance sheet is not a trading table. It is produced once per period,
//     signed, kept for as long as the companies act says, and restored as a unit when an
//     auditor asks about a number from three years ago. Its own schema is what lets a DBA
//     grant, back up and retain it separately from the seventeen projects underneath it.
//   * A schema-qualified name cannot collide. `fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM` is unambiguous even in a
//     database that also holds PNL_LINE, EXA_NET_EXPOSURE and LQV_FLOW, all of which are
//     present here through the includes below.
//   * It costs something, and the cost is worth naming: every reference to one of these
//     tables -- here, in mapping.pure, and in anything downstream -- must be
//     `[firm_balance_sheet::Store]fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.COLUMN`, four segments deep. Dropping the
//     `fbs.` produces an error that names the COLUMN and not the missing schema, which is the
//     commonest way a schema-owning project fails to compile.
//
// The three dependency stores put their tables in the DEFAULT schema, so every reference to
// one of theirs below has no schema segment at all. Both forms appear in the joins section.
//
// THE THREE INCLUDES, AND THE DIAMOND UNDERNEATH THEM. This store includes all three
// dependency stores and no others:
//
//    pnl_attribution::Store  -> position-keeping, valuation-core -> core-instrument,
//                               core-account, core-price, core-fx, core-types
//    exposure_agg::Store     -> credit-core, collateral-core -> core-party, core-ratings, ...
//    liquidity_view::Store   -> cash-core, funding-core -> core-account, core-tenor, core-types
//
// Seventeen projects arrive transitively and several arrive TWICE: core-account through both
// position-keeping and cash-core, core-types through both valuation-core and cash-core,
// core-party through credit-core and collateral-core. An include reaching the same database
// by two routes resolves to ONE database and nothing needs to be done about it. What would
// not be fine is `include core_account::Store` here as well -- a redundant include AND a
// reference to a project this one does not declare, which is exactly the defect the graph
// exists to detect. No `core_`, `position_keeping`, `valuation_core`, `credit_core`,
// `collateral_core`, `cash_core` or `funding_core` name appears anywhere in this file.
//
// THE AGGREGATION SHAPE, the other required construct: four `~groupBy` VIEWS at the foot of
// the schema, all over `fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM`, at four widths -- by category (what prints), by
// basis and side (the IFRS 9 disclosure), by book and side (the boundary), and by side alone
// (the balance check). `~groupBy` takes COLUMN references and nothing else, which is why
// FBS_LINE_ITEM carries SIDE, CATEGORY_CODE, BASIS_CODE and BOOK_CODE as stamped columns
// rather than anything derived. These are Legend views, not database views: no DDL, nothing
// seeds them, and the engine folds the GROUP BY into its SQL.
//
// Every join condition is on ONE line. A wrapped one compiles, but scripts/corpus/model.py
// refuses it, and these files are meant to stay readable by it.
//
// Every table is FBS_ and lives in `fbs`; every join is Fbs_; every filter is Fbs. Filter
// names are a GLOBAL namespace across the whole graph, so an unprefixed `AssetRows` here
// would fail all fifty-odd projects with a message naming the id and not this file.
//
// Money is NUMERIC because a balance sheet has to reconcile to the last unit. Rates, ratios
// and percentages are FLOAT because they are compared against a threshold rather than for
// equality. `REAL` is not used anywhere: it parses, compiles, and cannot be read back at
// execution (docs/UPSTREAM_FINDINGS.md F53).
//
// Tables are declared and unseeded. No ###Data element, no Runtime.
Database firm_balance_sheet::Store
(
   include pnl_attribution::Store
   include exposure_agg::Store
   include liquidity_view::Store

   Schema fbs
   (
      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- the statement ------

      // One published balance sheet. The composite key is the only sensible one: the same
      // institution on the same date has a different statement in each reporting currency,
      // and none of them is the "real" one.
      Table FBS_STATEMENT
      (
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3) PRIMARY KEY,
         BASIS_OF_PREPARATION VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         CONSOLIDATION_SCOPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         STATEMENT_STATUS VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
         RUN_ID VARCHAR(40),
         // pnl-attribution's batch id, so the P&L that fed retained earnings is nameable.
         PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID VARCHAR(24),
         // liquidity-view keys its ratios on a currency column of its own; this is the value
         // used when joining out, held separately because a statement may report the ratio
         // for a currency it is not itself denominated in.
         NSFR_SCENARIO_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3),
         TOTAL_ASSETS NUMERIC(24,2),
         TOTAL_LIABILITIES NUMERIC(24,2),
         TOTAL_EQUITY NUMERIC(24,2),
         PREPARED_BY VARCHAR(60),
         PREPARED_AT TIMESTAMP,
         SIGNED_OFF_ON DATE
      )

      // The batch. EXPOSURE_RUN_ID and PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID are the two upstream batches this
      // one consumed: a statement that moved because exposure-agg reran is a different
      // story from one that moved because the accounting changed, and without both ids on
      // the row there is no way to tell which happened.
      Table FBS_RUN
      (
         RUN_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         RUN_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         RUN_STATUS VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
         STARTED_AT TIMESTAMP,
         COMPLETED_AT TIMESTAMP,
         LINE_COUNT INTEGER,
         REJECTED_LINE_COUNT INTEGER,
         EXPOSURE_RUN_ID VARCHAR(40),
         PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID VARCHAR(24),
         TRIGGERED_BY VARCHAR(60)
      )

      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- the line grain -----

      // THE CENTRAL FACT, and the table all four views group. One table for all three sides,
      // narrowed into subtypes by FbsAssetRows / FbsLiabilityRows / FbsEquityRows at the foot
      // of this file; a column belonging to a side a row is not on is simply null.
      //
      // SIDE, CATEGORY_CODE, BASIS_CODE and BOOK_CODE are all stamped rather than derived,
      // because `~groupBy` names columns and cannot name an expression. They are also the
      // four axes anybody actually reads a balance sheet along.
      //
      // Note what is NOT here: no instrument name, no counterparty name, no rating. Every one
      // of those is reachable by join into one of the three dependencies, and a copy of it on
      // this row would be the stale value that ends up in a published statement.
      Table FBS_LINE_ITEM
      (
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3) NOT NULL,
         // ASSET, LIABILITY, EQUITY. The subtype discriminator and a `~groupBy` axis.
         SIDE VARCHAR(12) NOT NULL,
         CATEGORY_CODE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         // AC, FVOCI, FVTPL.
         BASIS_CODE VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         // TRADING, BANKING.
         BOOK_CODE VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
         FAIR_VALUE_LEVEL VARCHAR(4),
         CARRYING_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         GROSS_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         IMPAIRMENT_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         PRIOR_CARRYING_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         LOCAL_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3),
         LOCAL_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         FX_RATE FLOAT,
         RUN_ID VARCHAR(40),

         // ---- ASSET rows only, read by [fbsAssetLine].
         IS_HQLA BIT,
         HQLA_LEVEL_CODE VARCHAR(8),
         ENCUMBERED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         LIQUIDITY_DAYS INTEGER,
         HQLA_HOLDING_ID VARCHAR(40),

         // ---- LIABILITY rows only, read by [fbsLiabilityLine].
         MATURITY_DATE DATE,
         IS_SECURED BIT,
         FUNDING_TYPE VARCHAR(24),
         COUNTERPARTY_ID VARCHAR(40),
         IS_DEMAND_DEPOSIT BIT,

         // ---- EQUITY rows only, read by [fbsEquityLine].
         EQUITY_COMPONENT_CODE VARCHAR(24),
         IS_CET1_ELIGIBLE BIT,
         NON_CONTROLLING_INTEREST NUMERIC(24,2),

         // ---- the foreign key OUT of this project. Not mapped to a property: reached as an
         // object through Fbs_LineNetExposure.
         NET_EXPOSURE_ID VARCHAR(40)
      )

      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- the classifiers ----

      // PARENT_CODE is a plain column and there is deliberately no self-join on it: a
      // balance-sheet taxonomy has three levels and forty rows, and walking it in the model
      // costs nothing while a self-join costs every query that does not need it.
      Table FBS_CATEGORY
      (
         CATEGORY_CODE VARCHAR(24) PRIMARY KEY,
         CATEGORY_NAME VARCHAR(120) NOT NULL,
         PARENT_CODE VARCHAR(24),
         SIDE VARCHAR(12) NOT NULL,
         STATEMENT_ORDER SMALLINT,
         IS_SUBTOTAL BIT,
         NOTE_REFERENCE VARCHAR(12),
         RETIRED_ON DATE
      )

      // MOVEMENTS_THROUGH is the whole of IFRS 9 in one column: 'PL', 'OCI' or 'NONE'.
      Table FBS_MEASUREMENT_BASIS
      (
         BASIS_CODE VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
         BASIS_NAME VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL,
         STANDARD_REFERENCE VARCHAR(24),
         MOVEMENTS_THROUGH VARCHAR(12) NOT NULL,
         IS_FAIR_VALUE BIT,
         REQUIRES_ECL BIT,
         RECYCLES_TO_PL BIT
      )

      Table FBS_BOOK_CLASSIFICATION
      (
         BOOK_CODE VARCHAR(16) PRIMARY KEY,
         BOOK_NAME VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL,
         INTENT VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,
         IS_TRADING BIT,
         DEFAULT_BASIS_CODE VARCHAR(20),
         CAPITAL_TREATMENT VARCHAR(24),
         BOUNDARY_POLICY_REF VARCHAR(60)
      )

      Table FBS_FAIR_VALUE_LEVEL
      (
         LEVEL_CODE VARCHAR(4) PRIMARY KEY,
         LEVEL_NAME VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,
         INPUT_TYPE VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,
         IS_OBSERVABLE BIT,
         REQUIRES_DISCLOSURE BIT,
         LEVEL_RANK SMALLINT
      )

      // ------------------------------------------------- trading book vs banking book ------

      // Keyed on LINE_ID, one-to-one with an FBS_LINE_ITEM row: the trading detail is its own
      // table rather than thirteen more columns on the line because it is read on its own,
      // by a different desk, at a different time of day.
      //
      // The four columns after LINE_ID are pnl-attribution's primary key minus the
      // attribution id, which is the fifth. Together they are Fbs_TradingPositionPnlLine.
      Table FBS_TRADING_POSITION
      (
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         ACCOUNT_NO VARCHAR(34),
         // VARCHAR(60), matching pnl-attribution's own width. The wider of two candidate
         // widths is the only one that cannot truncate.
         INSTRUMENT_ID VARCHAR(60),
         COB_DATE DATE,
         PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID VARCHAR(24),
         QUANTITY NUMERIC(20,6),
         FAIR_VALUE NUMERIC(24,2),
         DAY_ONE_PROFIT NUMERIC(24,2),
         BID_OFFER_RESERVE NUMERIC(24,2),
         MODEL_RESERVE NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_LONG BIT,
         DESK_CODE VARCHAR(20)
      )

      Table FBS_BANKING_ASSET
      (
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48) PRIMARY KEY,
         PRODUCT_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         ORIGINATION_DATE DATE,
         MATURITY_DATE DATE,
         GROSS_CARRYING_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         EFFECTIVE_INTEREST_RATE FLOAT,
         UNAMORTISED_PREMIUM NUMERIC(24,2),
         ACCRUED_INTEREST NUMERIC(24,2),
         // 1, 2 or 3. The single column that decides twelve-month against lifetime ECL.
         ECL_STAGE SMALLINT,
         ALLOWANCE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_PURCHASED_CREDIT_IMPAIRED BIT,
         NET_EXPOSURE_ID VARCHAR(40)
      )

      // ------------------------------------------- derivatives, before any netting ---------

      Table FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET
      (
         DERIVATIVE_ASSET_ID VARCHAR(48) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         NETTING_SET_ID VARCHAR(40),
         NET_EXPOSURE_ID VARCHAR(40),
         COUNTERPARTY_ID VARCHAR(40),
         PRODUCT_CLASS VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         NOTIONAL NUMERIC(24,2),
         GROSS_POSITIVE_VALUE NUMERIC(24,2),
         CVA_ADJUSTMENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         FVA_ADJUSTMENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_CLEARED BIT,
         CURRENCY VARCHAR(3),
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      Table FBS_DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY
      (
         DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY_ID VARCHAR(48) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         NETTING_SET_ID VARCHAR(40),
         NET_EXPOSURE_ID VARCHAR(40),
         COUNTERPARTY_ID VARCHAR(40),
         PRODUCT_CLASS VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         NOTIONAL NUMERIC(24,2),
         GROSS_NEGATIVE_VALUE NUMERIC(24,2),
         DVA_ADJUSTMENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         FVA_ADJUSTMENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_CLEARED BIT,
         CURRENCY VARCHAR(3),
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      // COMPOSITE KEY on set and date: an offset restruck tomorrow is a new row, because the
      // statement that was published was published on the old one.
      Table FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT
      (
         NETTING_SET_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         GROSS_ASSET_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         GROSS_LIABILITY_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         OFFSET_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         NET_ASSET_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         NET_LIABILITY_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_BALANCE_SHEET_NETTED BIT,
         // 'IAS32' or 'ASC815'. The same book is a different size under each.
         OFFSET_BASIS VARCHAR(24),
         LEGAL_OPINION_REF VARCHAR(60)
      )

      Table FBS_COLLATERAL_OFFSET
      (
         OFFSET_ID VARCHAR(48) PRIMARY KEY,
         NETTING_SET_ID VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL,
         // exposure-agg's EXA_COLLATERAL_POSITION key. Held, not copied: the haircut, the
         // issuer and the asset class all stay on their side of the boundary.
         POSITION_ID VARCHAR(40),
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         CASH_COLLATERAL_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         SECURITIES_COLLATERAL_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         OFFSET_APPLIED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_CASH BIT,
         CURRENCY VARCHAR(3),
         REHYPOTHECATED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2)
      )

      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- HQLA by level ------

      // COMPOSITE KEY of four, which is deliberately the grain liquidity-view's LCR result
      // is keyed at minus the scenario: institution, date, level, currency. SCENARIO_ID is a
      // column rather than a key part because the balance-sheet stock does not depend on the
      // stress; only the ratio it feeds does.
      Table FBS_HQLA_STOCK
      (
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         HQLA_LEVEL_CODE VARCHAR(8) PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3) PRIMARY KEY,
         BALANCE_SHEET_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         UNENCUMBERED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         HAIRCUT_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         WEIGHTED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         // What the L2 cap threw away. Real assets, real liquidity, no regulatory credit.
         CAP_EXCESS_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         HOLDING_COUNT INTEGER,
         SCENARIO_ID VARCHAR(20)
      )

      // ------------------------------------ goodwill, intangibles, and the deductions ------

      Table FBS_GOODWILL
      (
         GOODWILL_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         CASH_GENERATING_UNIT VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL,
         ACQUISITION_DATE DATE,
         GROSS_GOODWILL NUMERIC(24,2),
         ACCUMULATED_IMPAIRMENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         CARRYING_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         RECOVERABLE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         LAST_TESTED_ON DATE,
         DISCOUNT_RATE FLOAT,
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      Table FBS_INTANGIBLE
      (
         INTANGIBLE_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         INTANGIBLE_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         COST_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         ACCUMULATED_AMORTISATION NUMERIC(24,2),
         CARRYING_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         USEFUL_LIFE_YEARS SMALLINT,
         IS_INTERNALLY_GENERATED BIT,
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      // The reconciling table between accounting equity and regulatory capital. Both
      // DEDUCTED_AMOUNT and RISK_WEIGHTED_REMAINDER are on one row because a threshold
      // deduction takes some of the balance and risk-weights the rest, and reporting only
      // the deducted half understates the exposure.
      Table FBS_CAPITAL_DEDUCTION
      (
         DEDUCTION_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         DEDUCTION_CODE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         // CET1, AT1, T2.
         DEDUCTION_TIER VARCHAR(8) NOT NULL,
         BALANCE_SHEET_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         THRESHOLD_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         DEDUCTED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         RISK_WEIGHTED_REMAINDER NUMERIC(24,2),
         REGULATION_REFERENCE VARCHAR(60),
         IS_FULLY_DEDUCTED BIT,
         GOODWILL_ID VARCHAR(40),
         INTANGIBLE_ID VARCHAR(40),
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- provisions ---------

      Table FBS_PROVISION
      (
         PROVISION_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         PROVISION_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         OPENING_BALANCE NUMERIC(24,2),
         CHARGE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         UTILISED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         RELEASED_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         CLOSING_BALANCE NUMERIC(24,2),
         EXPECTED_SETTLEMENT_DATE DATE,
         IS_DISCOUNTED BIT,
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      Table FBS_ECL_ALLOWANCE
      (
         ALLOWANCE_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         ECL_STAGE SMALLINT NOT NULL,
         PORTFOLIO_CODE VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,
         GROSS_EXPOSURE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         TWELVE_MONTH_ECL NUMERIC(24,2),
         LIFETIME_ECL NUMERIC(24,2),
         ALLOWANCE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         MODEL_CODE VARCHAR(24),
         // The credit committee's overlay, held apart so it cannot be read as modelled.
         POST_MODEL_ADJUSTMENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         NET_EXPOSURE_ID VARCHAR(40)
      )

      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- the equity ---------

      Table FBS_EQUITY_COMPONENT
      (
         COMPONENT_CODE VARCHAR(24) PRIMARY KEY,
         COMPONENT_NAME VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL,
         COMPONENT_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         CAPITAL_TIER VARCHAR(8),
         IS_DISTRIBUTABLE BIT,
         IS_RECYCLABLE BIT,
         PRESENTATION_ORDER SMALLINT
      )

      // COMPOSITE KEY of four, matching FBS_STATEMENT's three plus the component.
      Table FBS_EQUITY_BALANCE
      (
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         COMPONENT_CODE VARCHAR(24) PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3) PRIMARY KEY,
         OPENING_BALANCE NUMERIC(24,2),
         MOVEMENT_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         CLOSING_BALANCE NUMERIC(24,2),
         ATTRIBUTABLE_TO_PARENT NUMERIC(24,2),
         NON_CONTROLLING_INTEREST NUMERIC(24,2),
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48)
      )

      Table FBS_OCI_RESERVE
      (
         RESERVE_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         RESERVE_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         BASIS_CODE VARCHAR(20),
         GROSS_RESERVE NUMERIC(24,2),
         DEFERRED_TAX NUMERIC(24,2),
         NET_RESERVE NUMERIC(24,2),
         RECYCLED_TO_PL NUMERIC(24,2),
         IS_RECYCLABLE BIT,
         COMPONENT_CODE VARCHAR(24)
      )

      // Keyed exactly as FBS_STATEMENT: one roll-forward per statement, no more.
      Table FBS_RETAINED_EARNINGS
      (
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3) PRIMARY KEY,
         OPENING_RETAINED NUMERIC(24,2),
         PROFIT_FOR_PERIOD NUMERIC(24,2),
         DIVIDENDS_DECLARED NUMERIC(24,2),
         OTHER_MOVEMENTS NUMERIC(24,2),
         CLOSING_RETAINED NUMERIC(24,2),
         PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID VARCHAR(24),
         IS_VERIFIED BIT
      )

      // ---------------------------------------------------------------- control ------------

      Table FBS_ADJUSTMENT
      (
         ADJUSTMENT_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         LINE_ID VARCHAR(48) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         ADJUSTMENT_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         ADJUSTMENT_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         REASON VARCHAR(400),
         RAISED_BY VARCHAR(60),
         RAISED_ON DATE,
         APPROVED_BY VARCHAR(60),
         APPROVED_ON DATE,
         REVERSED_ON DATE
      )

      Table FBS_BALANCE_CHECK
      (
         CHECK_ID VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY,
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE NOT NULL,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY VARCHAR(3) NOT NULL,
         CHECK_TYPE VARCHAR(24) NOT NULL,
         LEFT_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         RIGHT_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         DIFFERENCE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         TOLERANCE_AMOUNT NUMERIC(24,2),
         SEVERITY VARCHAR(12),
         DETECTED_AT TIMESTAMP,
         RESOLVED_ON DATE,
         OWNER VARCHAR(60)
      )

      Table FBS_ATTESTATION
      (
         INSTITUTION_ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         ROLE_CODE VARCHAR(24) PRIMARY KEY,
         ATTESTED_BY VARCHAR(60),
         ATTESTED_AT TIMESTAMP,
         ATTESTATION_STATUS VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
         COMMENTARY VARCHAR(400),
         WITHDRAWN_ON DATE
      )

      // ==================================================================================
      // THE AGGREGATION SHAPE -- four `~groupBy` views over fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM
      // ==================================================================================
      // `~groupBy` comes FIRST, before the columns, and names COLUMNS only -- never an
      // expression. Every grouping column is repeated as a PRIMARY KEY output column,
      // because the mapping's `~primaryKey` has to name the grain the view produces.
      //
      // Inside a schema the references are schema-qualified on BOTH sides: the `~groupBy`
      // list and every column source say `fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM`. A view declared inside the
      // schema is itself schema-qualified for everything downstream, so the mapping says
      // `[firm_balance_sheet::Store]fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.TOTAL_CARRYING`.
      //
      // A group with no rows FORMS NO GROUP and is absent, not zero. A category with nothing
      // in it on a date simply does not appear.

      // The statement as printed: one row per category per statement.
      View FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL
      (
         ~groupBy
         (
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CATEGORY_CODE
         )
         INSTITUTION_ID: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY PRIMARY KEY,
         CATEGORY_CODE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CATEGORY_CODE PRIMARY KEY,
         LINE_COUNT: count(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID),
         TOTAL_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_GROSS: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.GROSS_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_IMPAIRMENT: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.IMPAIRMENT_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_PRIOR_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.PRIOR_CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         // max and min beside the sum, because a category total of zero built from two
         // enormous opposite numbers is not a total of zero in any useful sense.
         LARGEST_LINE: max(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         SMALLEST_LINE: min(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT)
      )

      // The IFRS 9 disclosure: how much of each side is at AC, at FVOCI and at FVTPL.
      // Grouped by basis AND side, because the netted answer is meaningless.
      View FBS_BASIS_TOTAL
      (
         ~groupBy
         (
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BASIS_CODE,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE
         )
         INSTITUTION_ID: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY PRIMARY KEY,
         BASIS_CODE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BASIS_CODE PRIMARY KEY,
         SIDE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE PRIMARY KEY,
         LINE_COUNT: count(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID),
         TOTAL_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_GROSS: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.GROSS_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_IMPAIRMENT: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.IMPAIRMENT_AMOUNT),
         LARGEST_LINE: max(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT)
      )

      // The book boundary in money. Drops the currency on purpose: the boundary is a capital
      // question and capital is measured in one currency per institution.
      View FBS_BOOK_TOTAL
      (
         ~groupBy
         (
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BOOK_CODE,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE
         )
         INSTITUTION_ID: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         BOOK_CODE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BOOK_CODE PRIMARY KEY,
         SIDE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE PRIMARY KEY,
         LINE_COUNT: count(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID),
         TOTAL_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_PRIOR_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.PRIOR_CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         LARGEST_LINE: max(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT)
      )

      // THE BALANCE CHECK ITSELF. Three rows per statement -- ASSET, LIABILITY, EQUITY --
      // straight off the line table, with nothing between the identity and the data.
      // FBS_STATEMENT.TOTAL_ASSETS is what was published; this is what the lines say.
      View FBS_SIDE_TOTAL
      (
         ~groupBy
         (
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY,
            fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE
         )
         INSTITUTION_ID: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID PRIMARY KEY,
         AS_OF_DATE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE PRIMARY KEY,
         REPORTING_CURRENCY: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY PRIMARY KEY,
         SIDE: fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE PRIMARY KEY,
         LINE_COUNT: count(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID),
         TOTAL_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CARRYING_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_GROSS: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.GROSS_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_IMPAIRMENT: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.IMPAIRMENT_AMOUNT),
         TOTAL_PRIOR_CARRYING: sum(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.PRIOR_CARRYING_AMOUNT)
      )
   )

   // ==========================================================================================
   // JOINS INSIDE THE `fbs` SCHEMA -- both sides schema-qualified, one line each
   // ==========================================================================================

   // The line to its statement, on all three key columns. Two of them would join a sterling
   // line to a dollar statement.
   Join Fbs_LineStatement(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY)
   Join Fbs_LineCategory(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CATEGORY_CODE = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY.CATEGORY_CODE)
   Join Fbs_LineBasis(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BASIS_CODE = fbs.FBS_MEASUREMENT_BASIS.BASIS_CODE)
   Join Fbs_LineBook(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BOOK_CODE = fbs.FBS_BOOK_CLASSIFICATION.BOOK_CODE)
   Join Fbs_LineFairValueLevel(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.FAIR_VALUE_LEVEL = fbs.FBS_FAIR_VALUE_LEVEL.LEVEL_CODE)
   Join Fbs_LineRun(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.RUN_ID = fbs.FBS_RUN.RUN_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineAdjustment(fbs.FBS_ADJUSTMENT.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineTradingPosition(fbs.FBS_TRADING_POSITION.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineBankingAsset(fbs.FBS_BANKING_ASSET.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineGoodwill(fbs.FBS_GOODWILL.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineIntangible(fbs.FBS_INTANGIBLE.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineDeduction(fbs.FBS_CAPITAL_DEDUCTION.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineProvision(fbs.FBS_PROVISION.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineEquityBalance(fbs.FBS_EQUITY_BALANCE.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineDerivativeAsset(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)
   Join Fbs_LineDerivativeLiability(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY.LINE_ID = fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.LINE_ID)

   Join Fbs_StatementRun(fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.RUN_ID = fbs.FBS_RUN.RUN_ID)
   Join Fbs_StatementBalanceCheck(fbs.FBS_BALANCE_CHECK.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_BALANCE_CHECK.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_BALANCE_CHECK.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY)
   // Two columns only: an attestation is of the statement, not of one currency cut of it, so
   // every currency statement for a date shares the same signatures.
   Join Fbs_StatementAttestation(fbs.FBS_ATTESTATION.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_ATTESTATION.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE)
   Join Fbs_StatementRetainedEarnings(fbs.FBS_RETAINED_EARNINGS.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_RETAINED_EARNINGS.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_RETAINED_EARNINGS.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY)
   Join Fbs_StatementHqlaStock(fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY)
   Join Fbs_StatementEquityBalance(fbs.FBS_EQUITY_BALANCE.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_EQUITY_BALANCE.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_EQUITY_BALANCE.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY)

   // The netting hub: both derivative sides land on the same (set, date) row, which is the
   // only place in this project where the gross asset and the gross liability meet.
   Join Fbs_DerivativeAssetNetting(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.NETTING_SET_ID = fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.NETTING_SET_ID and fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.AS_OF_DATE)
   Join Fbs_DerivativeLiabilityNetting(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY.NETTING_SET_ID = fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.NETTING_SET_ID and fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.AS_OF_DATE)
   Join Fbs_NettingCollateralOffset(fbs.FBS_COLLATERAL_OFFSET.NETTING_SET_ID = fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.NETTING_SET_ID and fbs.FBS_COLLATERAL_OFFSET.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.AS_OF_DATE)

   Join Fbs_BookDefaultBasis(fbs.FBS_BOOK_CLASSIFICATION.DEFAULT_BASIS_CODE = fbs.FBS_MEASUREMENT_BASIS.BASIS_CODE)
   Join Fbs_OciReserveBasis(fbs.FBS_OCI_RESERVE.BASIS_CODE = fbs.FBS_MEASUREMENT_BASIS.BASIS_CODE)
   Join Fbs_OciReserveComponent(fbs.FBS_OCI_RESERVE.COMPONENT_CODE = fbs.FBS_EQUITY_COMPONENT.COMPONENT_CODE)
   Join Fbs_EquityBalanceComponent(fbs.FBS_EQUITY_BALANCE.COMPONENT_CODE = fbs.FBS_EQUITY_COMPONENT.COMPONENT_CODE)
   Join Fbs_DeductionGoodwill(fbs.FBS_CAPITAL_DEDUCTION.GOODWILL_ID = fbs.FBS_GOODWILL.GOODWILL_ID)
   Join Fbs_DeductionIntangible(fbs.FBS_CAPITAL_DEDUCTION.INTANGIBLE_ID = fbs.FBS_INTANGIBLE.INTANGIBLE_ID)
   // The banking asset to its allowance, on the credit key both rows carry.
   Join Fbs_BankingAssetEcl(fbs.FBS_BANKING_ASSET.NET_EXPOSURE_ID = fbs.FBS_ECL_ALLOWANCE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID)

   // ---- into the four aggregation views -----------------------------------------------------
   // Each of these crosses into a GROUP BY, never into another line. Navigating
   // `line.sideTotal` reaches the group the line is IN and not a sibling row.
   Join Fbs_LineCategoryTotal(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.REPORTING_CURRENCY and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.CATEGORY_CODE = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.CATEGORY_CODE)
   Join Fbs_LineBasisTotal(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_BASIS_TOTAL.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_BASIS_TOTAL.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_BASIS_TOTAL.REPORTING_CURRENCY and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BASIS_CODE = fbs.FBS_BASIS_TOTAL.BASIS_CODE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE = fbs.FBS_BASIS_TOTAL.SIDE)
   Join Fbs_LineBookTotal(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_BOOK_TOTAL.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_BOOK_TOTAL.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BOOK_CODE = fbs.FBS_BOOK_TOTAL.BOOK_CODE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE = fbs.FBS_BOOK_TOTAL.SIDE)
   Join Fbs_LineSideTotal(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.REPORTING_CURRENCY and fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.SIDE)
   // From the statement into two of the views, so a reader gets the printed lines and the
   // balance check without touching FBS_LINE_ITEM at all.
   Join Fbs_StatementCategoryTotal(fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.REPORTING_CURRENCY)
   Join Fbs_StatementSideTotal(fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.REPORTING_CURRENCY = fbs.FBS_SIDE_TOTAL.REPORTING_CURRENCY)
   // And from the three classifiers into their own totals, so "everything at FVTPL" is one
   // navigation from the basis rather than a scan of the line table.
   Join Fbs_CategoryCategoryTotal(fbs.FBS_CATEGORY.CATEGORY_CODE = fbs.FBS_CATEGORY_TOTAL.CATEGORY_CODE)
   Join Fbs_BasisBasisTotal(fbs.FBS_MEASUREMENT_BASIS.BASIS_CODE = fbs.FBS_BASIS_TOTAL.BASIS_CODE)
   Join Fbs_BookBookTotal(fbs.FBS_BOOK_CLASSIFICATION.BOOK_CODE = fbs.FBS_BOOK_TOTAL.BOOK_CODE)

   // ==========================================================================================
   // THE JOINS THAT LEAVE THIS PROJECT -- sixteen of them, five hops from a leaf
   // ==========================================================================================
   // Legal only because of the three `include`s at the top. Every one lands on a table or a
   // VIEW owned by a DIRECT dependency: PNL_ is pnl-attribution's, EXA_ is exposure-agg's,
   // LQV_ is liquidity-view's. None is schema-qualified on the far side, because all three
   // of those projects put their tables in the default schema; ours are, because we did not.
   //
   // Note what is NOT here. There is no join to CA_ACCOUNT, CI_INSTRUMENT, CP_LEGAL_ENTITY or
   // CT_CURRENCY. All four are reachable -- the includes drag seventeen projects in -- and
   // naming any of them would be a reference to a project this one does not declare. The
   // model navigates `$line.netExposure.counterparty` and `$position.pnlLine.position`
   // instead, which is the dependency's own association and costs this project nothing.

   // ---- into pnl-attribution -----------------------------------------------------------------
   // FIVE COLUMNS, which is exactly PNL_LINE's primary key. This is the deepest single
   // reference in the graph: PNL_LINE is itself the apex of pnl-attribution's diamond over
   // position-keeping and valuation-core, each of which sits on core-instrument, core-account,
   // core-price and core-fx, each of which sits on core-types. Five hops.
   Join Fbs_TradingPositionPnlLine(fbs.FBS_TRADING_POSITION.PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID = PNL_LINE.ATTRIBUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_TRADING_POSITION.INSTITUTION_ID = PNL_LINE.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_TRADING_POSITION.ACCOUNT_NO = PNL_LINE.ACCOUNT_NO and fbs.FBS_TRADING_POSITION.INSTRUMENT_ID = PNL_LINE.INSTRUMENT_ID and fbs.FBS_TRADING_POSITION.COB_DATE = PNL_LINE.COB_DATE)
   // Into pnl-attribution's own `~groupBy` VIEW: the firm's whole day of P&L as one row.
   // View-to-row, from two different tables, because both the statement and the retained
   // earnings roll-forward need the same number and neither should recompute it.
   Join Fbs_StatementPnlRunTotal(fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID = PNL_RUN_TOTAL.ATTRIBUTION_ID)
   Join Fbs_RetainedEarningsPnlRunTotal(fbs.FBS_RETAINED_EARNINGS.PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID = PNL_RUN_TOTAL.ATTRIBUTION_ID)
   Join Fbs_RunPnlRun(fbs.FBS_RUN.PNL_ATTRIBUTION_ID = PNL_RUN.ATTRIBUTION_ID)

   // ---- into exposure-agg --------------------------------------------------------------------
   Join Fbs_LineNetExposure(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.NET_EXPOSURE_ID = EXA_NET_EXPOSURE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID)
   Join Fbs_BankingAssetNetExposure(fbs.FBS_BANKING_ASSET.NET_EXPOSURE_ID = EXA_NET_EXPOSURE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID)
   Join Fbs_EclNetExposure(fbs.FBS_ECL_ALLOWANCE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID = EXA_NET_EXPOSURE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID)
   Join Fbs_DerivativeAssetNetExposure(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.NET_EXPOSURE_ID = EXA_NET_EXPOSURE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID)
   Join Fbs_DerivativeLiabilityNetExposure(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY.NET_EXPOSURE_ID = EXA_NET_EXPOSURE.NET_EXPOSURE_ID)
   // The legal answer to what may be offset. This project reads enforceability; it does not
   // re-derive it.
   Join Fbs_NettingAdjustmentNettingSet(fbs.FBS_NETTING_ADJUSTMENT.NETTING_SET_ID = EXA_NETTING_SET.NETTING_SET_ID)
   Join Fbs_DerivativeAssetNettingSet(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.NETTING_SET_ID = EXA_NETTING_SET.NETTING_SET_ID)
   Join Fbs_DerivativeLiabilityNettingSet(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_LIABILITY.NETTING_SET_ID = EXA_NETTING_SET.NETTING_SET_ID)
   Join Fbs_CollateralOffsetPosition(fbs.FBS_COLLATERAL_OFFSET.POSITION_ID = EXA_COLLATERAL_POSITION.POSITION_ID)
   // Into exposure-agg's `~groupBy` VIEW: this counterparty's whole day, one row.
   Join Fbs_DerivativeAssetCounterpartyDayNet(fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.COUNTERPARTY_ID = EXA_COUNTERPARTY_DAY_NET.COUNTERPARTY_ID and fbs.FBS_DERIVATIVE_ASSET.AS_OF_DATE = EXA_COUNTERPARTY_DAY_NET.AS_OF_DATE)
   Join Fbs_RunExposureRun(fbs.FBS_RUN.EXPOSURE_RUN_ID = EXA_RUN.RUN_ID)

   // ---- into liquidity-view ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Join Fbs_HqlaStockLevel(fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.HQLA_LEVEL_CODE = LQV_HQLA_LEVEL.LEVEL_CODE)
   // Four columns, which is exactly LQV_LCR_RESULT's key. REPORTING_CURRENCY meets
   // CURRENCY_CODE: the two projects name the same fact differently and the join is where
   // that is reconciled, once, rather than in every query.
   Join Fbs_HqlaStockLcrResult(fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.INSTITUTION_ID = LQV_LCR_RESULT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.REPORTING_CURRENCY = LQV_LCR_RESULT.CURRENCY_CODE and fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.AS_OF_DATE = LQV_LCR_RESULT.AS_OF_DATE and fbs.FBS_HQLA_STOCK.SCENARIO_ID = LQV_LCR_RESULT.SCENARIO_ID)
   Join Fbs_AssetLineHqlaHolding(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.HQLA_HOLDING_ID = LQV_HQLA_HOLDING.HOLDING_ID)
   Join Fbs_StatementNsfrResult(fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.INSTITUTION_ID = LQV_NSFR_RESULT.INSTITUTION_ID and fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.NSFR_SCENARIO_CURRENCY = LQV_NSFR_RESULT.CURRENCY_CODE and fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.AS_OF_DATE = LQV_NSFR_RESULT.AS_OF_DATE)

   // ==========================================================================================
   // FILTERS -- a GLOBAL namespace, so every one is Fbs-prefixed
   // ==========================================================================================
   // The three applied ones are the subtype discriminators, referenced from the mapping as
   // [firm_balance_sheet::Store]FbsAssetRows. Not one filter here is a boolean literal:
   // `Filter X(T.IS_HQLA = true)` fails to parse with `Unexpected token 'true'`, so a flag is
   // tested as a string comparison against a code column or as a null test.
   //
   // Unlike regulatory-extract's overlapping regime/state filters, these three are DISJOINT
   // and exhaustive: a row is on exactly one side of a balance sheet, which is the one place
   // in accounting where a three-way split really is a partition.
   Filter FbsAssetRows(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE = 'ASSET')
   Filter FbsLiabilityRows(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE = 'LIABILITY')
   Filter FbsEquityRows(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.SIDE = 'EQUITY')

   // Declared and unapplied, for a downstream project to reference.
   Filter FbsOpenBalanceChecks(fbs.FBS_BALANCE_CHECK.RESOLVED_ON is null)
   Filter FbsLiveCategories(fbs.FBS_CATEGORY.RETIRED_ON is null)
   Filter FbsLiveAdjustments(fbs.FBS_ADJUSTMENT.REVERSED_ON is null)
   Filter FbsCurrentAttestations(fbs.FBS_ATTESTATION.WITHDRAWN_ON is null)
   Filter FbsPublishedStatements(fbs.FBS_STATEMENT.SIGNED_OFF_ON is null)
   Filter FbsFairValuedLines(fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM.BASIS_CODE = 'FVTPL')
)
